---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Breadcrumbs from '../../components/Breadcrumbs.astro';
import ArticleCard from '../../components/ArticleCard.astro';
import { entryPath, getPublishedEntries } from '../../lib/content';
const entries = await getPublishedEntries();
const schema = { '@type': 'ProfilePage', name: 'MushroomScope Editorial Team', url: Astro.url.href, mainEntity: { '@type': 'Organization', '@id': 'https://mushroomscope.com/#organization', name: 'MushroomScope', url: 'https://mushroomscope.com/', email: 'hello@mushroomscope.com' } };
---
<BaseLayout title="MushroomScope Editorial Team & Review Process" description="Learn what the MushroomScope organizational byline means, how articles are researched, and which review limitations apply." schema={schema}>
  <div class="shell py-8"><Breadcrumbs items={[{ label: 'About', href: '/about/' }, { label: 'MushroomScope Editorial Team' }]} /></div>
  <article class="shell max-w-4xl py-12"><p class="eyebrow">Organizational author profile</p><h1 class="mt-4 font-serif text-5xl sm:text-6xl">MushroomScope Editorial Team</h1><div class="prose mt-8"><p>This byline identifies research, writing, illustration, and maintenance performed for MushroomScope. It does not represent a named mycologist, clinician, or dietitian.</p><h2>Research process</h2><p>Articles are structured from taxonomic databases, government guidance, university extension resources, peer-reviewed literature, and specialist references appropriate to the topic. Sources are displayed on each page so readers can inspect them.</p><ol><li>Define the page’s practical question and safety boundary.</li><li>Collect primary and authoritative sources that directly address that question.</li><li>Separate observed facts from interpretation, preliminary evidence, and unknowns.</li><li>Check names, quantities, instructions, citations, internal links, and image provenance.</li><li>Run structured-content validation and a complete production build before publication.</li></ol><h2>Review disclosure</h2><p>Editorial review checks source relevance, uncertainty, internal consistency, and safety language. A page is labeled expert reviewed only when a named qualified reviewer, review date, and review scope can be disclosed. MushroomScope does not invent credentials or imply expert review where none occurred.</p><h2>Ownership and commercial independence</h2><p>MushroomScope is an independent educational publishing project. Advertising or affiliate relationships, if introduced, will be disclosed and will not give a commercial partner control over editorial conclusions.</p><h2>Corrections</h2><p>Report factual concerns to <!--email_off--><a href="mailto:hello@mushroomscope.com">hello@mushroomscope.com</a><!--/email_off-->. Include the page URL, disputed statement, and supporting source when possible. Confirmed substantive corrections update the page and its modification date.</p></div></article>
  <section class="shell pb-20"><h2 class="font-serif text-3xl">Published work</h2><div class="mt-6 grid gap-6 md:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-3">{entries.slice(0, 12).map((entry) => <ArticleCard title={entry.data.title} description={entry.data.description} category={entry.data.category} href={entryPath(entry)} image={entry.data.coverImage} imageAlt={entry.data.coverAlt} />)}</div><p class="mt-8"><a href="/sitemap/">Browse all published guides →</a></p></section>
</BaseLayout>
